  "provider_query": "Public Telegram web preview of the official Telegram channel",
  "answer": "The official Telegram channel is **@telegram** (“Telegram News”). Its public web preview (no app or account required) is:\n\n1. **Channel preview (latest posts):** https://t.me/s/telegram — described as “The official Telegram on Telegram.” ([t.me/s/telegram](https://t.me/s/telegram))\n\nRelated public links:\n\n2. **Join / profile link:** https://t.me/telegram — cited in Telegram’s Channels FAQ as the official example (e.g. t.me/telegram). ([telegram.org/faq_channels](https://telegram.org/faq_channels))\n\n3. **How public channel web views work:** Telegram says public channel content can be seen on the web without an account and is indexed by search engines; example format given is `t.me/s/…`. ([telegram.org/tour/channels](https://telegram.org/tour/channels))\n\n4. **Embed a public post:** Open a post’s `t.me` link in a browser and use **Embed** (example pattern: `t.me/durov/43`). ([core.telegram.org/widgets/post](https://core.telegram.org/widgets/post))\n\n5. **Telegram blog (source of many channel posts):** https://telegram.org/blog ([telegram.org/blog](https://telegram.org/blog))\n\n6. **Web client (not a channel preview):** https://web.telegram.org/k/ and https://web.telegram.org/a/ ([instantview.telegram.org](https://instantview.telegram.org/templates/telegram.org/))\n\n7. **Username link format:** `t.me/<username>` (also `telegram.me`). ([core.telegram.org/api/links](https://core.telegram.org/api/links))\n\n8. **Official channels tour:** points readers to the official **@Telegram** channel for product updates. ([telegram.org/tour/channels](https://telegram.org/tour/channels))",
